// E525 — a primitive type isn't an affliction.
//
// A misfortune is a named, described thing; a bare Teaghrán carries no
// reason and no fields. Same argument as E213 one level up: the type
// doesn't name enough to serve the role.
//
// Practical reason too: allowing it would mark Teaghrán as an affliction
// module-wide, and every unrelated "má" mixing Teaghrán with something
// else would meet at an afflicted type nobody asked for.

feidhm ainmnigh(aitheantas: Uimhir) -> Teaghrán ar Teaghrán {
    "duine"
}